==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|engenious||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵenh₁-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|ingénieux}}, from {{der|en|fro|engenious}}, from {{der|en|la|ingeniōsus|t=endowed with good natural capacity, gifted with genius}}, from {{m|la|ingenium|t=innate or natural quality, natural capacity, genius}}, from {{af|la|in-|t1=in|gignere|t2=to produce|nocat=1}}, {{der|en|itc-ola|genere}}. See also {{m|en|engine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈdʒiːnjəs/|/ɪnˈdʒiːniəs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ingenious.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːniəs|s=4}}
* {{hyph|en|in|ge|nious}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of a [[person#Noun|person]]: [[display#Verb|Displaying]] [[genius#Noun|genius]] or [[brilliance]]; [[inventive]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:intelligent}}
#: {{ux|en|This fellow is '''ingenious'''; he fixed a problem I didn’t even know I had.}}
# Of a [[thing]]: [[characterize]]d by genius; [[cleverly]] [[contrive]]d or [[do#Verb|done]].
#: {{ux|en|That is an '''ingenious''' model of the atom.}}
# [[show#Verb|Showing]] [[originality]] or [[sagacity]]; [[witty]].
#: {{synonyms|en|adroit|keen|sagacious|shrewd|Thesaurus:witty}}
#: {{ux|en|He sent me an '''ingenious''' reply to an email.}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Francesca Carrara|volume=I|page=147|passage=I have scarcely recovered the surprise of the '''ingenious''' question, before I meet another surprise in the still more '''ingenious''' answer}}

====Usage notes====
Not to be confused with {{m|en|ingenuous}}.

